    ('なんて（なんと）','A phrase used as the colloquial version of なんと.','A phrase used as the colloquial version of なんと.'),
    ('〜なんて（感情・評価）','A colloquial particle used to express a strong feeling such as astonishment, incredulousness, envy, disdain, dislike, happiness, etc.','A colloquial particle used to express a strong feeling such as astonishment, incredulousness, envy, disdain, dislike, happiness, etc.'),
    ('〜に（も）なく','A phrase that means something unusual happens or someone does something unusual.','A phrase that means something unusual happens or someone does something unusual.'),
    ('〜に/ともなると','A phrase that is used when something or some situation is perceived to be special.','A phrase that is used when something or some situation is perceived to be special.'),
    ('〜にいたっては','A compound particle that indicates an extreme example.','A compound particle that indicates an extreme example.'),
    ('〜にかかわらず・に関/拘/係わらず','A compound particle that means “regardless of”','A compound particle that means “regardless of”'),
    ('〜にかけては','A compound particle that marks something in which someone excels or has conﬁdence.','A compound particle that marks something in which someone excels or has conﬁdence.'),
